-- Passage rg5-figurative-language-p01
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('80aa67a6-66ba-5905-ac37-bf7cd62dc883', 'rg5-figurative-language-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-figurative-language'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Cello Recital$q$, $q$Priya Raman had practiced her cello piece for six weeks. On the night of the recital, her stomach was a nest of fluttering moths. She peeked out from behind the curtain. The audience looked as big as an ocean.

Her teacher, Mr. Okonkwo, noticed her pale face. "Practice makes perfect," he reminded her. "You have played this piece a hundred times. Your fingers know the way home."

Priya walked onto the stage and sat down. She took a deep breath and drew the bow across the strings. The first note was shaky, but the second was stronger. Soon the music flowed like a calm river.

Halfway through, she forgot one measure. For a moment, her mind went blank. Then she remembered her teacher's advice to keep going no matter what. She picked up the melody and finished with a long, sweet note.

The crowd burst into applause. Priya stood and took a bow, smiling so wide that her cheeks hurt. Backstage, her little brother Dev hugged her. "You were on fire!" he said.

Priya laughed. Her nervous feeling had vanished, and in its place was a calm, proud glow.$q$, 'draft')
