   $q$In paragraph 1, Priya's "stomach was a nest of fluttering moths." What does this metaphor show?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She saw insects flying near the stage.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"She had eaten too much before the show.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She felt very nervous before playing.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She felt calm and ready to perform.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She felt very nervous before playing.$q$, $q$Fluttering moths stand for the jumpy feeling of nerves, and the next sentences show her peeking out at a huge audience. There are no real moths in the story.$q$, 'draft', '80aa67a6-66ba-5905-ac37-bf7cd62dc883')
