   $q$In paragraph 2, the coach says, "Slow and steady wins the race." What does this proverb mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The slowest runner always finishes in first place.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"Keeping an even pace works better than rushing.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Runners should sprint as fast as they can at the start.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Runners should stop to rest a few times in a race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Keeping an even pace works better than rushing.$q$, $q$Tomas stays "near the middle of the pack" so he will not tire too early, which shows the saying is about a steady pace. It does not mean the slowest runner wins.$q$, 'draft', 'cfb1b150-5387-51a1-aa1b-7e4b31000d9a')
